{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985529-one-more-question-requirement","id":985529,"title":"One more question /requirement","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-11T11:17:16-07:00","id":985529,"title":"One more question /requirement","content":"So covering up wyrm taint...how does one go about that? Spirit, life I'm sure..but what others? Havent seen anything like it in HWYDT or anywhere else,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:08:07-07:00","id":985620,"title":"","content":"Wyrm taint is a paradicmatic expression of Resonance.<br /> So it could be either of:<br /> Spirit 1<br /> Mind 1<br /> Prime 1(+Mind)<br /> Entropy 1.<br /> <br /> Just don't expect the same results the garou next to you gets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:22:31-07:00","id":985625,"title":"","content":"no i just want to show up as not tainted. not high and mighty or what not. So you are basically saying this is no different than changing ones aura?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:25:50-07:00","id":985630,"title":"","content":"There's a few possibilities, which are dependent on the degree and &quot;type&quot;, so to speak, of (T)aint...<br /> <br /> Spirit:2/3: If the taint is essentially wholly spiritual -- it has virtually no physical manifestation, such as with a &quot;properly&quot; corrupted Garou/Dancer, Fomori, a vampire who is undead physically, et al), then the sense of the corruption can be clouded via Spirit:2 &quot;fuguing&quot; the perception of it in a manner similar to strengthening or occluding the Gauntlet. Similarly, many &quot;active&quot; manifestations of it -- spiritual &quot;contagion&quot;, actively &quot;disturbing&quot; resonances of (S)pirit, et al -- can be clouded/suppressed via Spirit:3, just as most spiritual forces can be lulled at that level. (These applications/levels are useful for Garou who have high Corruption ratings -- 7+ -- who would sense as Wyrm but have not yet fully succumb to the Wyrm nor &quot;properly&quot; become BSDs; S:2 is useful for thwarting &quot;casual scanning&quot; -- that is, act as an opposed threshold vs. Sense Wyrm or some similar power -- while S:3 would be better vs. a more deep probing.)<br /> <br /> Spirit:2/3, Life:3/4 : If the taint also has physical manifestations, then Life must be added. (3 to heal/restore &quot;simple&quot; corruption that is more akin to &quot;damage&quot;/an ongoing disease -- leaking puss, some physical distortion/bloating that can occur due to trauma/what-have-you, while 4 would be needed for proper transformative properties -- bat wings, super-huge fangs, tentacles with poison suckers, etc...)<br /> <br /> Spirit:2/3, Life:3/4, Mind:3/4 : If the taint has also seriously distorted the target's mind/mental processes, then Mind needs to be added to disguise/obscure the corruption (3) or attempt to blend it so seamlessly into the subconscious as to resist persistent scanning (4).<br /> <br /> Spirit:2/3, Life:3/4, Mind:3/4, Entropy:5 : As with the above, but by adding E:5, the &quot;trail&quot; that the target leaves behind (physically, metaphysically, and spiritually) can be similarly fugued/suppressed. E:5 distorts even the perception of after-evidence concerning revealing any Wyrm-taint he may have, whether directly or tangentially, by both redirecting circumstances that would cause such a reveal as well as muting (E)ntropic &quot;tell-tail&quot; signatures he leaves behind.<br /> <br /> Spirit:2/3, Correspondence:3, Time:2, Entropy:2 : A more subtle/less overt deception. By muting/removing the spiritual link between the target and his own (C)orruption (S:2/3, C:3), a fairly resistant veil can be made vs. detection. By adding T:2 and E:2, any scrying of the target's past to note when (C)orruption may have occurred (at a given instance and/or as a gradual process) can be similarly occluded (and, with S and C in place with it, a relatively plausible &quot;false past&quot; can be maintained relative to the &quot;present&quot;, which links with T an E for past scanning; this combo fails, however, vs. a more broadly &quot;temporally aware/existing&quot; entity/force, such as a mage who is himself time-traveling &quot;forward&quot; from a past wherein he has firsthand knowledge of the target's taint, or a Time:6+ entity (especially a paradox spirit like Wrinkle) who exists outside of conventional time as it is understood. Both of those cases, however, are relatively fringe circumstances. Note further, too, that this combo doesn't do anything to disguise current physical -- and spirit-made-manifest -- taint that might exist when observed directly; it only distorts the mystical sensing/ scanning of it. An important distinction...)<br /> <br /> Prime:2/3, Life:3/4, Entropy:4 : A side-step method for those who aren't spiritually skilled. Prime can act as a means of &quot;warping around&quot; the sense of metaphysical corruption that the target may have (acting as a basic &quot;counterspell&quot;, of sorts, vs. detection, though this leaves many detectors with the sense of deliberate countermeasures being made -- Per + Awareness would likely suss things out); Life again works around any physical issues, while Entropy guides both circumstances as well as Prime in the manner necessary to occlude the sense of (C)orruption. (This approach works as a basic line of countermeasure but falls short vs. any sustained or particularly astute detection.)<br /> <br /> Prime:4, Mind:4 : by constantly &quot;cleansing&quot; the soul/metaphysical Pattern of the target, the sense of taint can be effectively hidden. Mind not only disguises thought/(R)esonance, meshing the (C)orruption into highly subtle thought patterns, but also actively causes any detecting characters to &quot;look the other way&quot; relative to the taint that they do find (but then &quot;forget&quot; about a moment later). Prime in this case both supports the Mind aspect, metaphysically, but also provides the sense of &quot;cleansing&quot; that makes the (R)esonance less-than-detectable. (While Prime:5 is normally needed to &quot;wash out/distort&quot;, properly, a living pattern, the presumed willingness on the target's part to not be detected allows for P:4 to do the trick, while also effectively &quot;counter-spelling&quot; aspects of any detecting magics, as well, but again with M's help making such dispelling less-than-noticeable.)<br /> <br /> <br /> I could list some more, but I need to get back to other stuff. This should give you a good framework to build off of.... Hope it helps!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}